{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CNN-RNN Image Captioning.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CNN-RNN Image Captioning.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cnn rnn image captioning cnn rnn image captioning","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CNN-RNN Image Captioning.md","fileName":"CNN-RNN Image Captioning.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CNN-RNN Image Captioning","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 02:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Recurrent Sequence Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recurrent Sequence Architecture","Convolutional Neural Network","Encoder-Decoder Network","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CNN-RNN Image Captioning.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CNN-RNN Image Captioning.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cnn rnn image captioning cnn rnn image captioning","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CNN-RNN Image Captioning.md","fileName":"CNN-RNN Image Captioning.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CNN-RNN Image Captioning","heading":"CNN-RNN Image Captioning","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An image-captioning model can combine a [[Convolutional Neural Network]] encoder with a recurrent language decoder. The CNN analyzes the image and produces a vector representation; the recurrent component uses that vector as context while generating a description word by word.\n\nKelleher presents this as an intermodal variant of an [[Encoder-Decoder Network]]: the input is visual, but the output is a language sequence. The useful abstraction is not that a fixed vector perfectly captures an image's meaning; it is that learned representations can connect two different data forms in one trainable architecture.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recurrent Sequence Architecture","Convolutional Neural Network","Encoder-Deco